From: PiSight <pisight@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: exclude GHS generator header from bootstrap

The bootstrap executable does not link the GHS generator implementation.
Including its header on Linux instantiates factory methods that reference
unlinked symbols, so host-cmake fails to link. The full CMake build still
includes the generator normally.

--- a/Source/cmake.cxx
+++ b/Source/cmake.cxx
@@ -129,8 +129,10 @@
 
 // NOTE: the __linux__ macro is predefined on Android host too, but
 // main CMakeLists.txt filters out this generator by host name.
-#if (defined(__linux__) && !defined(__ANDROID__)) || defined(_WIN32)
-#  include "cmGlobalGhsMultiGenerator.h"
+#if !defined(CMAKE_BOOTSTRAP)
+#  if (defined(__linux__) && !defined(__ANDROID__)) || defined(_WIN32)
+#    include "cmGlobalGhsMultiGenerator.h"
+#  endif
 #endif
 
 #if defined(__APPLE__)
